$ The Aeroelastic Analysis User's Guide's example HA144B (the BAH jet
$ transport wing) with the guide's divergence request (MSC's 2023.1 edition,
$ listing 3-1; Simcenter 2606's Table 2-2), rebuilt from the sorted bulk
$ data (MSC listing 7-8, Simcenter Table 6-10) for
$ test_nastran95ase_trim_corrections.m. AEROS SYMXZ is +1 here and -1 in
$ HA144B: the guide's divergence output (MSC listing 5-1, Simcenter p. 4-4;
$ the TPL's ha144h runs it with SYMXZ +1 too) is what symmetric
$ aerodynamics give, to 6-7 digits on every root; the antisymmetric deck's
$ roots are 15 % higher. Simcenter Nastran 2606 runs it as written and
$ prints those roots
$ (data/ha144b_diverg_symmetric_simcenter2606.f06; EIGC's root count ND0 is
$ its field 8).
ID GUIDE, HA144BD
SOL 144
CEND
TITLE = EXAMPLE HA144B: BAH JET TRANSPORT WING DYNAMIC ANALYSIS
SUBTI = DIVERGENCE ANALYSIS
LABEL = AILERON ROLL, STATIC AERO SOLUTION
  ECHO  = BOTH
  SPC   = 13 $ ANTISYMMETRIC CONSTRAINTS
  MPC   =  1 $ CONTROL SURFACE RELATIVE MOTION
  SET 2 = 7 THRU 12
  SET 3 = 11
  DISP  = 2
  SPCF  = 3
  AEROF = ALL
  APRES = ALL
  DIVERG = 100
  CMETHOD = 100
